# tasksel machinery + tasks — debian-cd's update_tasks needs task-desktop and
# tasksel-data present in the CD mirror to build the task structure and derive
# the default desktop; task-kde-desktop pulls the full KDE closure the preseed's
# `tasksel/first ... kde-desktop` selects at install time (all of it offline).
tasksel
tasksel-data
task-desktop
task-kde-desktop
kde-plasma-desktop
sddm
konsole
dolphin
firefox-esr
network-manager
sudo
lvm2
grub-efi-amd64
efibootmgr
linux-image-6.12.0
linux-headers-6.12.0
sovereign-os-cockpit
python3
python3-yaml
python3-jsonschema
prometheus-node-exporter
curl
git
nano
# debian-cd's installtools step wants the installation guide present in the pool
installation-guide-amd64
# trixie's base-installer installs `zstd` as part of the base set (dpkg's default
# compressor), but nothing in the closure above depends on the zstd BINARY package
# (they pull libzstd1), so it was absent from the offline mirror and base-install
# failed with "Unable to install zstd". Pull it in explicitly.
zstd
